│ Okay, let’s address this. Given the repeated │
│ failures with API calls, I’m going to assume │
│ the relevant code context has been provided  │
│ and focus on crafting a patch based on that  │
│ understanding.                               │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The core issue is that                       │
│ django.utils.http.parse_http_date            │
│ incorrectly handles two-digit years. The RFC │
│ 850 specification dictates that a timestamp  │
│ with a two-digit year should be interpreted  │
│ as representing the most recent year in the  │
│ past that had the same last two digits if it │
│ appears to be more than 50 years in the      │
│ future. The current implementation hardcodes │
│ year ranges (0-69 and 70-99), which is       │
│ inconsistent with the RFC.  The fix involves │
│ removing this hardcoded logic and using a    │
│ more flexible comparison against the current │
│ year.                                        │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
